  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1000,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Scope and freshness",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Freshness rule: a current target is `up == 1` with sample age at most 90s. Missing or stale samples are unknown, never healthy and never zero. `up` is scrape availability only, not backend health.\n\nKubernetes inventory is a cached KSM observation, not strongly consistent API absence; use native kubectl for decisive absence checks. CNPG and Temporal Pods are shown as ordinary Pods. Container CPU/memory panels cover running workload containers only (no completed or pending containers, no infrastructure containers). Declared requests and limits are not usage."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1001,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Namespaces and Pods",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 201,
